## CHANGELOG
Golden rule throughout: every number calibrated from the game's own data, or omitted — never fabricated.
- **S24c (v1.0.23) — i18n restore bug: chrome stayed Chinese after switching back to English (owner-reported).**
  ROOT CAUSE: `_i18nTextNode`'s fast-skip `if(!cur||!/[A-Za-z]/.test(cur))return;` ran BEFORE the lang branch, so
  during RESTORE (LANG='en') any node whose current text is pure Chinese (no Latin — i.e. every translated label
  like 总览 / 断开连接) returned early and never restored. Only the persistent CHROME was hit (header/nav/gate/
  footer/modals) because tab content re-renders fresh in the active language; chrome is never re-rendered, so it
  stuck in Chinese. FIX (one function): the Latin fast-skip now lives INSIDE the `LANG==='zh'` branch and tests the
  English ORIGINAL — the restore branch is never Latin-gated. `_i18nAttrs` was already correct (its guard was
  already scoped to the translate branch). Verified in-preview: load-in-zh → en, en→zh→en, all 11 tabs + chrome =
  0 leftover Chinese (only the 中 toggle label + its intentionally bilingual title remain, by design). Present since
  v1.0.21 (the i18n debut). See [[tbh-i18n-language-switch]].
- **S24b (v1.0.22) — desktop mini-HUD packaging fix (owner: "mini-HUD … not even working in the web app or
  the installed version?").** ROOT CAUSE: `mini.html` was never in electron-builder's `files` glob (only
  `src/**/*` + `dashboard.html` + `package.json`), so `miniWin.loadFile('../mini.html')` opened a BLANK window
  in every installer since v1.0.16 — it only worked under `npm start` (runs from source, not the asar). FIX:
  added `"mini.html"` to `build.files`; rebuilt + verified `\mini.html` is now inside `app.asar`. Also clarified
  (CHANGELOG + here) that the mini-HUD is **DESKTOP-ONLY** by design — a browser can't float an always-on-top
  window over a fullscreen game, so the 🗗 button only exists in Electron (gated on `window.tbhNative.miniToggle`);
  its absence in the web app is correct, not a bug.
- **S24 (v1.0.20 + v1.0.21) — difficulty-labeled stages + an English/简体中文 language switch.** (v1.0.20)
  Owner report: the leaderboard showed the meaningless **"Act 12-5"**. The save numbers stages CONTINUOUSLY across
  the game's **4 difficulty bands** (Normal/Nightmare/Hell/Torment, 3 acts × 10 each), so `stageActLabel`/`stageLabel`
  (both engines) now decode the band: `2205 → "Act 3-5 · Torment"`. Calibrated from the game's OWN data — the 4
  `Difficulty_*` localization keys + the 4 difficulty Soulstones (`ItemName_190001-4`), and the 116-stage
  `OfflineRewardInfoData` total = exactly 30+30+30+26 (Torment's last act is short). The Crew board re-decodes from
  the authoritative numeric `maxStage` key (`crewStage()`), so members on older clients show the new form too.
  Verified against the live save (current Normal 3-9 / max Normal 3-10) — there was NO confirmed Nightmare+ data
  point, so the band map is corroborated (not save-verified past Normal); confirm on the owner's first Nightmare clear.
