- **S21 (v1.0.15) — extremely-slow-update fix (root-caused on the owner's install).** Evidence: the updater cache
  held the previous installer + blockmap and the 1.0.14 download sat at a 0-byte temp file → it was running a
  DIFFERENTIAL download. Measured on the same line: full-stream from GitHub releases = ~1.0 MB/s (79 MB ≈ 76 s),
  ranged requests = ~68 ms each — and our NSIS exe is solid-compressed, so any change ripples through the whole
  archive: the "diff" ≈ the full 79 MB fetched as THOUSANDS of sequential range requests = many minutes. Fixes:
  (a) `autoUpdater.disableDifferentialDownload = true` (main.js — arrives with this update for all future ones);
  (b) `nsis.differentialPackage: false` — releases stop shipping a .blockmap, so EXISTING 1.0.13/1.0.14 installs
  immediately fall back to the fast full download when fetching v1.0.15 (no blockmap → no differential attempt);
  (c) the update banner now shows transferred/total MB + live MB/s so a big download never looks stuck.
